`--dry-run` changes only whether the file is written, never what is computed. The same artifact is
run twice — dry, then wet — and the two JSON documents below differ in exactly one character, the
`written` flag. The second run stamping at all is itself the proof that the first did not: the
already-stamped guard would have skipped it otherwise, and no `--force` is passed.

Arithmetic, s-golf: one turn, 08:00:00 → 08:05:00 = 300s = 5 minutes; tokens input 9, output 4, no
cache fields = 0; model claude-fx-haiku.

